-- Q3432: IT Infrastructure and Architecture [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Reduced hardware costs due to fewer network devices needed","Simplified network troubleshooting from a single broadcast domain","Faster data transfer speeds between all connected devices","Unrestricted lateral movement for any compromised device on the network"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-53 SC-7 (Boundary Protection), a flat network with no segmentation allows any compromised device unrestricted lateral movement across the entire broadcast domain. Without internal boundaries, malware or an attacker on one workstation can directly reach financial servers and databases.
Wrong (A): Reduced hardware costs may be true but represent a benefit, not a risk of flat network design.
Wrong (B): Simplified troubleshooting is an operational advantage, not a security risk.
Wrong (C): Faster data transfer is a potential performance benefit, not a risk finding for the auditor.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3432;

