-- Q3463: IT Infrastructure and Architecture [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Strangler fig pattern with an anti-corruption layer","Complete cloud migration replacing the legacy mainframe","Monolithic deployment consolidating all services together","Serverless computing using event-driven function execution"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per COBIT 2019 BAI03, the strangler fig pattern gradually replaces legacy functionality with modern services while maintaining an anti-corruption layer that translates between old and new system interfaces. This enables incremental modernization without a high-risk big-bang migration.
Wrong (B): A complete cloud migration replaces the legacy system entirely rather than maintaining parallel operation with an integration layer.
Wrong (C): Monolithic deployment consolidates everything into a single application, which is the opposite of the microservices approach described.
Wrong (D): Serverless computing is an execution model, not an architectural migration pattern for legacy-to-modern integration.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3463;

