-- Q3474: ERP and Accounting Information Systems [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Role-based access controls separating vendor, invoice, and payment functions","Requiring the clerk to use a strong and complex password","Adding a CAPTCHA challenge to the vendor creation form","Encrypting the entire accounts payable database at rest"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-53 AC-5, role-based access controls enforce segregation of duties by restricting users to defined roles with non-overlapping permissions. Separating vendor creation, invoice entry, and payment approval into distinct roles prevents a single individual from executing an end-to-end fraudulent transaction.
Wrong (B): Strong passwords authenticate user identity but do not restrict what authorized users can do within the system.
Wrong (C): CAPTCHA verifies that the user is human but does not address the segregation-of-duties weakness.
Wrong (D): Database encryption protects data at rest from unauthorized access but does not prevent the clerk from performing incompatible duties.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3474;
